WEBVTT

00:00:39.494 --> 00:00:41.083
Hey!

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:46.797
Fry, mon, if you're going
to be living in the office,

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.924
you could at least
be on time for work.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.425
I'm sorry.

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:52.803
I was up really late
poking through people's desks.

00:00:56.198 --> 00:00:57.199
All right, people,

00:00:57.224 --> 00:01:00.352
I will now outline
today's 12-point agenda.

00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:03.188
We'll begin with point one...

00:01:09.711 --> 00:01:11.755
...Concerning our pest problem.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.257
Somebody's
been leaving food around

00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:15.884
and it's attracting owls.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:20.180
And I, for one, am getting tired
of cleaning those owl traps.

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:23.684
Now...

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.978
As this shocking graph indicates,

00:01:26.061 --> 00:01:29.773
our water consumption
has tripled in the last month.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.567
Now, I notice
Fry has been here for a month

00:01:32.651 --> 00:01:34.319
so I'm appointing him
head of a committee

00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:35.946
to find
who's responsible.

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:37.489
Fry?

00:01:41.994 --> 00:01:43.287
Am I cracking up

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.371
or is Fry's living here

00:01:44.454 --> 00:01:46.164
starting to get in the way of bus...

00:01:52.587 --> 00:01:54.256
What the hell are you doing?

00:01:54.339 --> 00:01:56.383
You're getting
a huge dose of radiation.

00:01:56.466 --> 00:01:58.218
And great lift.

00:01:58.302 --> 00:02:00.470
Do you know how long it's going to take me

00:02:00.554 --> 00:02:02.389
to recalibrate these engines?

00:02:02.681 --> 00:02:04.141
Hey, when you look this good,

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.018
you don't have to know anything.

00:02:07.102 --> 00:02:09.146
Professor, we need
to talk to you about Fry.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.023
That's right!
We want some money!

00:02:11.106 --> 00:02:12.774
Wait, what's this about Fry?

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.276
He's a nice guy

00:02:14.359 --> 00:02:16.570
but we think it's about time
he got his own place.

00:02:16.653 --> 00:02:17.738
Oh, fuff.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.823
He's not causing any trouble.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.534
Now, if you don't mind,
I'm rather busy.

00:02:22.618 --> 00:02:24.828
I seem to have mislaid
my alien mummy.

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:28.248
This sarcophagus
should contain the remains

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:30.208
of Emperor Nimbala, who ruled

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:33.128
Zuben Five
over 29 million years ago.

00:02:33.211 --> 00:02:34.504
Hey, professor.

00:02:34.588 --> 00:02:36.965
Mmm. Great jerky.

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:38.133
Mmm.

00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:40.844
My God, this is an outrage.

00:02:41.224 --> 00:02:43.203
I was going to eat that mummy.

00:02:43.339 --> 00:02:45.549
Fry has got to go.

00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:51.021
Bachelor chow,now with flavor.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.106
...And bigfoot is down!

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.350
Sheesh. 40,000 channels

00:02:55.433 --> 00:02:58.687
and only 150 of them
have anything good on.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:01.314
All My Circuits
is brought to you by...

00:03:01.418 --> 00:03:03.003
Robo Fresh.

00:03:03.066 --> 00:03:05.527
Designed by a robot for a robot.

00:03:08.363 --> 00:03:11.783
I've been processing this
for some time, Monique,

00:03:11.867 --> 00:03:14.035
and, well... Will you marry me?

00:03:14.119 --> 00:03:15.203
Oh, Calculon!

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:25.422
It fits!

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.965
Then you must know that I'm...

00:03:27.048 --> 00:03:28.800
Metric? I've always known.

00:03:28.884 --> 00:03:32.262
But for you, my darling,
I'm willing to convert.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.687
Hmm, must be a friend of theirs.

00:03:38.829 --> 00:03:41.855
Fry, we've got to discuss
your living arrangements.

00:03:41.938 --> 00:03:43.523
We've all talked it over, and...

00:03:43.607 --> 00:03:44.816
Hey, All My Circuits.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.234
Move over.

00:03:49.154 --> 00:03:50.064
Ah!

00:03:50.213 --> 00:03:52.257
Fry, sometimes in close quarters

00:03:52.341 --> 00:03:55.385
people do inconsiderate things
without realizing it.

00:03:55.469 --> 00:03:56.928
I know, but I forgive you.

00:03:57.054 --> 00:03:58.847
No, Fry, by "close quarters"

00:03:58.930 --> 00:03:59.973
I mean this office.

00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:01.391
Uh-huh.

00:04:01.475 --> 00:04:03.685
- And by "people," I mean you.
- Right.

00:04:03.769 --> 00:04:05.562
And by "inconsiderate,"
I mean...

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.522
Leela,
we're trying to watch TV.

00:04:07.606 --> 00:04:10.233
Yeah. Would you kindly
shut your noise hole?

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.488
So who's
that weird-looking guy?

00:04:14.571 --> 00:04:15.947
That's a human.

00:04:16.031 --> 00:04:17.991
- What's he do?
- Usual human stuff.

00:04:18.075 --> 00:04:21.119
He laughs, he learns,
he loves.

00:04:21.203 --> 00:04:22.621
Boring.

00:04:24.039 --> 00:04:26.958
Calculon?
I thought you were in a coma.

00:04:27.042 --> 00:04:29.211
That's what I wanted you to think

00:04:29.294 --> 00:04:31.171
with your soft, human brain.

00:04:31.254 --> 00:04:33.924
Hey, uh, why
is the TV getting smaller?

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.554
We'll bill you for the couch.

00:04:46.001 --> 00:04:47.688
Cheer up, meat bag.

00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:49.398
You barely touched your amoeba.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:52.567
It looked good,
but I just don't feel like eating.

00:04:52.651 --> 00:04:55.404
- You want it?
- Nah, I'm trying to watch my input.

00:04:55.529 --> 00:04:59.324
I need plenty of wholesome,
nutritious alcohol.

00:04:59.408 --> 00:05:03.412
The chemical energy
keeps my fuel cells charged.

00:05:03.886 --> 00:05:05.054
What are the cigars for?

00:05:05.455 --> 00:05:07.165
They make me look cool.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.293
Oh, I can't believe
they threw me out like that.

00:05:10.377 --> 00:05:12.337
I must have been
really acting like a jerk.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.486
Yeah, but everybody's a jerk.
You, me, this jerk.

00:05:17.551 --> 00:05:19.219
That's my philosophy.

00:05:19.302 --> 00:05:21.722
So, where are you going to stay?

00:05:21.847 --> 00:05:23.306
I don't know.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.892
Do refrigerators still
come in cardboard boxes?

00:05:26.018 --> 00:05:28.437
Yeah, but the rents are outrageous.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.105
Why don't you
just come move in with me?

00:05:30.188 --> 00:05:32.274
Really? That would be great!

00:05:32.566 --> 00:05:34.860
You sure I won't be imposing?

00:05:34.943 --> 00:05:37.237
Nah. I've always wanted a pet.

00:05:46.496 --> 00:05:48.248
Here we are, your new home.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.001
Cool. You know,
I've never even seen

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.336
a robot's apartment before.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:54.880
Come on in. I'll give you the tour.

00:06:07.059 --> 00:06:08.727
Let's see, where to start.

00:06:09.227 --> 00:06:11.188
Okay.
This is the TV area.

00:06:11.271 --> 00:06:13.231
That over there is the breakfast nook.

00:06:13.523 --> 00:06:15.525
And over here is where you'll be living,

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:18.511
which is great, 'cause till now
it's just been wasted space.

00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:20.489
It's kind of cramped in here.

00:06:20.572 --> 00:06:22.616
I don't even have room
to hang my clothes.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.910
Look, pal, you've only got
one set of clothes

00:06:24.993 --> 00:06:27.204
and you're not taking them off
while I'm here.

00:06:29.206 --> 00:06:31.041
Well, I'm bushed.
Good night.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.377
Wait. Bender? Bender?

00:06:37.172 --> 00:06:40.550
Kill all humans. Kill all humans.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.135
Must kill all...

00:06:43.212 --> 00:06:45.423
Bender, wake up!

00:06:45.806 --> 00:06:48.558
I was having
the most wonderful dream.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.414
I think you were in it.

00:06:50.519 --> 00:06:52.437
Uh... Uh, listen, Bender, uh...

00:06:52.938 --> 00:06:54.314
Where's your bathroom?

00:06:54.564 --> 00:06:55.732
- Bath what?
- Bathroom.

00:06:55.875 --> 00:06:57.376
- What room?
- Bathroom.

00:06:57.401 --> 00:06:58.402
What, what?

00:06:58.485 --> 00:07:00.195
Ah, never mind.

00:07:00.278 --> 00:07:01.947
Mmm...

00:07:06.215 --> 00:07:08.634
Hey, sexy mama...

00:07:08.996 --> 00:07:11.123
Want to kill all humans?

00:07:20.723 --> 00:07:22.559
We sure are cheerful
this morning.

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:25.512
Yeah, this past week with Fry's
been a blast.

00:07:25.595 --> 00:07:28.473
You know, beneath his warm,
sunny exterior

00:07:28.557 --> 00:07:31.601
beats the cold, mechanical heart
of a robot.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.896
What happened to you?

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:36.773
Oh, it's Bender's apartment.

00:07:36.857 --> 00:07:39.860
He put in carpeting yesterday
and now my head hits the ceiling.

00:07:39.943 --> 00:07:42.696
Hey, do you realize you're
standing at a weird angle?

00:07:42.779 --> 00:07:44.781
Now you're okay.

00:07:44.865 --> 00:07:46.700
Look at yourself, you're a wreck.

00:07:46.783 --> 00:07:49.119
You've got to find a new place to live.

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:51.413
Is that an invitation?

00:07:51.496 --> 00:07:52.789
Love your optimism, Fry.

00:07:52.873 --> 00:07:56.209
But seriously, you've got to
tell Bender you're moving out.

00:07:56.335 --> 00:07:58.253
Yeah, but he might get kind of upset.

00:07:58.378 --> 00:07:59.769
I don't think I can do that to him.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:02.007
Hey, there's my little space heater.

00:08:05.802 --> 00:08:06.803
Well, I'm moving out.

00:08:06.887 --> 00:08:08.388
What?

00:08:08.555 --> 00:08:09.765
I'm sorry, Bender,

00:08:09.848 --> 00:08:11.808
but there's just not enough room.

00:08:11.892 --> 00:08:12.934
Not enough room?

00:08:13.018 --> 00:08:14.811
My place is two cubic meters

00:08:15.312 --> 00:08:17.356
and we only take up 1.5 cubic meters.

00:08:17.856 --> 00:08:20.817
We've got room for a whole
'nother two-thirds of a person.

00:08:21.109 --> 00:08:24.529
What if I just help the two of you
find a bigger apartment?

00:08:24.821 --> 00:08:26.031
I don't know.

00:08:26.114 --> 00:08:28.492
I've got a lot of great memories
in my old place.

00:08:29.951 --> 00:08:31.244
And now they're gone.

00:08:34.831 --> 00:08:39.336
Sure, it ain't one of them
la-de-da above-ground places

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:42.881
but if you like dank...
Forget about it.

00:08:42.964 --> 00:08:45.050
At least it's got a great view.

00:08:45.717 --> 00:08:47.177
- Aah!
- What the...?

00:08:53.392 --> 00:08:55.811
'Scuse me. I got to go
change a lightbulb.

00:09:00.716 --> 00:09:03.677
Wow. Now, this
is fantastic.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.637
Hmm, I'm not sure
we want to pay

00:09:05.721 --> 00:09:07.848
for a dimension we're
not going to use.

00:09:07.931 --> 00:09:09.975
Aah! Ooh! Ee!
Ooh! Oh! Aah! Ee!

00:09:10.058 --> 00:09:13.228
Ooh! Aah! Ee! Aah!
Ooh! Ee! Ooh! Ee! Aah!

00:09:13.312 --> 00:09:14.771
Ooh! Ee! Ooh!

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.838
Well, I give up.
What's the catch?

00:09:20.903 --> 00:09:22.029
Oh, no catch.

00:09:22.154 --> 00:09:24.448
Although we are
technically in New Jersey.

00:09:24.531 --> 00:09:27.117
Not one place even remotely livable.

00:09:27.618 --> 00:09:29.369
Oh, how awful.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.496
Did he at least die painlessly?

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.582
To shreds, you say.

00:09:33.665 --> 00:09:36.418
Well, how is his wife holding up?

00:09:36.501 --> 00:09:38.337
To shreds, you say.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.755
Very well, then.

00:09:40.464 --> 00:09:43.550
Sad, sad,
terrible, gruesome news

00:09:43.634 --> 00:09:46.011
about my colleague, Dr. Mobutu.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:48.764
Was his apartment rent controlled?

00:09:53.977 --> 00:09:56.230
Wow. This is beautiful.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.798
What's with all the crap?

00:09:58.248 --> 00:09:59.500
It's not crap.

00:09:59.583 --> 00:10:01.126
Dr. Mobutu collected this crap

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:04.797
while he was exploring
the whatchacallit... Universe.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.759
Well, this place has everything except
the only thing I care about... a TV.

00:10:08.842 --> 00:10:12.763
It's got a TV, you young
whatchacallit... Idiot.

00:10:14.098 --> 00:10:15.265
Ooh.

00:10:15.349 --> 00:10:16.558
Whoa, slow down.

00:10:16.642 --> 00:10:18.936
This place just
doesn't feel like home.

00:10:19.019 --> 00:10:20.729
It just isn't... Cozy.

00:10:24.691 --> 00:10:25.859
Ah...

00:10:26.026 --> 00:10:27.736
I can barely move.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.155
It's perfect!

00:11:19.663 --> 00:11:21.898
Man, it's a total sty.

00:11:22.176 --> 00:11:24.392
For the first time in 1,000 years

00:11:24.476 --> 00:11:26.103
I feel like I'm home.

00:11:26.186 --> 00:11:28.980
Yeah, it's going
to be fun on a bun.

00:11:29.064 --> 00:11:31.983
You know, Fry,
of all the friends I've had,

00:11:32.067 --> 00:11:33.360
you're the first.

00:11:38.824 --> 00:11:39.991
Hey, mon.

00:11:42.035 --> 00:11:43.787
Happy housewarming, Fry.

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:46.164
It's a miniature fruit salad tree.

00:11:46.498 --> 00:11:47.499
Ooh.

00:11:52.321 --> 00:11:53.322
Wah!

00:11:53.405 --> 00:11:54.740
- Hey, Amy.
- Hey.

00:11:55.908 --> 00:11:57.242
This is for you, Fry...

00:11:57.326 --> 00:11:58.702
Zevulon the great.

00:11:58.786 --> 00:12:00.496
He's teriyaki-style.

00:12:03.624 --> 00:12:05.334
Wow. Heavy-drinking crowd.

00:12:06.752 --> 00:12:08.462
I'd better go out for more beer.

00:12:08.954 --> 00:12:11.290
Hang on. All My Circuits
is about to start.

00:12:11.373 --> 00:12:14.334
I know, but I need alcohol
to power up my batteries.

00:12:14.626 --> 00:12:16.962
If Calculon's wedding
doesn't go just right

00:12:17.045 --> 00:12:19.715
I'll be emotionally
and electrically drained.

00:12:25.387 --> 00:12:27.306
Hey...

00:12:32.394 --> 00:12:33.937
These are mighty tasty.

00:12:34.021 --> 00:12:36.440
Thank you.
I made them myself.

00:12:38.734 --> 00:12:40.944
Shh. The wedding's about to start.

00:12:41.028 --> 00:12:42.988
If anyone here objects to this union,

00:12:43.507 --> 00:12:45.885
let them speak now
or forever hold their...

00:12:49.253 --> 00:12:50.796
Is he objecting or backing up?

00:12:50.898 --> 00:12:52.483
Looks like both.

00:12:52.548 --> 00:12:54.758
I'm afraid
my half-brother is correct.

00:12:54.842 --> 00:12:56.760
You see,
I have a terrible secret

00:12:56.844 --> 00:12:57.845
and that secret is...

00:12:59.054 --> 00:13:00.180
Oh, come on!

00:13:00.264 --> 00:13:02.141
Oh, fix it.

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.546
Hey, what happened to the TV?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.791
It just went out.

00:13:05.822 --> 00:13:08.283
This is an outrage.
I'm going to go yell at the manager.

00:13:10.399 --> 00:13:12.109
All right!

00:13:12.192 --> 00:13:14.236
Come back, Bender!
It's working!

00:13:14.319 --> 00:13:16.947
To reiterate,
my terrible secret is...

00:13:20.442 --> 00:13:21.935
It's out again.

00:13:22.076 --> 00:13:24.704
What? That's the last straw.

00:13:24.729 --> 00:13:26.815
It's back on!

00:13:29.818 --> 00:13:30.802
Pardon me.

00:13:30.827 --> 00:13:33.238
I don't mean to pry into
what you're doing in here

00:13:33.363 --> 00:13:35.365
with the crab and the one-eyed
lady and the Chinese girl,

00:13:35.718 --> 00:13:39.096
but everyone on this floor
is having trouble with their TV reception.

00:13:39.327 --> 00:13:41.913
Yeah, and you better
get rid of whatever's causing it

00:13:41.997 --> 00:13:43.456
or we're out of this dump.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.292
Relax, sonny.

00:13:45.375 --> 00:13:48.044
This cajigger'll find
the source of the interference.

00:14:05.562 --> 00:14:07.355
We want our TV back.

00:14:10.692 --> 00:14:12.402
There's your problem.

00:14:12.486 --> 00:14:14.779
Oh, my God.
Bender, it's your thingy.

00:14:17.199 --> 00:14:18.783
You people are nuts.

00:14:18.867 --> 00:14:21.850
My antenna never
interfered with my old TV.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.690
You had cable.
This is satellite.

00:14:24.773 --> 00:14:26.108
Obviously, your thoughts

00:14:26.191 --> 00:14:28.318
are being transmitted
on the same frequency.

00:14:28.402 --> 00:14:30.154
They're on my cell phone, too.

00:14:30.279 --> 00:14:32.865
Madame, I believe you're mistaken.

00:14:33.365 --> 00:14:36.076
Wow, that lady's got a huge ass.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.537
Those could be anyone's
thoughts, fat-ass.

00:14:40.247 --> 00:14:42.082
The robot has to go.

00:14:42.165 --> 00:14:43.750
Yeah!

00:14:44.498 --> 00:14:46.000
Well, you heard the mob.

00:14:46.461 --> 00:14:47.838
Fine. Come on, Fry.

00:14:47.921 --> 00:14:49.673
Let's move to that apartment

00:14:49.756 --> 00:14:50.377
that smelled like a sewer.

00:14:50.402 --> 00:14:52.071
You liked that one, right?

00:14:52.254 --> 00:14:53.672
Oh, it's tempting, but, well...

00:14:53.973 --> 00:14:56.304
I am already kind
of settled in here.

00:14:56.513 --> 00:14:59.015
Or we could live underground
with the mutants.

00:14:59.224 --> 00:15:01.643
A little fire'll show them who's boss.

00:15:01.935 --> 00:15:05.647
Uh... Listen, is there maybe
some way we could do this

00:15:05.731 --> 00:15:07.816
with you going and me not going?

00:15:07.899 --> 00:15:09.234
I don't understand.

00:15:09.317 --> 00:15:11.653
Well, you were going to
live in the closet anyway.

00:15:11.737 --> 00:15:13.780
Won't you be just as happy
back in your old place?

00:15:14.281 --> 00:15:16.825
But... Then
we wouldn't be roommates.

00:15:16.908 --> 00:15:19.870
I'll come visit sometime,
and you can visit me here.

00:15:19.953 --> 00:15:20.996
No, he can't.

00:15:21.346 --> 00:15:23.181
Anyway, I'm sure
it'll work out.

00:15:23.206 --> 00:15:25.167
This way we'll both be happy.

00:15:25.584 --> 00:15:28.045
Happy. Yeah, that's Bender.

00:15:28.128 --> 00:15:30.922
Always happy.

00:15:34.009 --> 00:15:36.637
Hey, the TV's back on!

00:15:36.961 --> 00:15:38.034
We are gathered to mourn

00:15:38.059 --> 00:15:39.435
the death of Calculon,

00:15:39.965 --> 00:15:42.885
industrialist, private eye, friend.

00:15:43.456 --> 00:15:46.000
Mind if I give the eulogy?

00:15:46.977 --> 00:15:49.230
Calculon! You're alive!

00:15:51.877 --> 00:15:54.171
Yay! Calculon's back!

00:15:56.256 --> 00:15:57.424
Right. So long.

00:15:57.716 --> 00:15:59.676
Good-bye.

00:15:59.885 --> 00:16:02.679
Do you think Calculon's evil twin
will ever walk again?

00:16:02.763 --> 00:16:05.182
I don't know, Amy.
I just don't know.

00:16:05.265 --> 00:16:07.684
- Wah!
- Hey, thanks for coming.

00:16:09.789 --> 00:16:11.207
Fry, you're Bender's best friend.

00:16:11.271 --> 00:16:13.273
How could you let that mob
kick him out?

00:16:13.357 --> 00:16:15.901
Aw, come on.
Bender loves mobs.

00:16:16.193 --> 00:16:18.195
Only when he's in them,
and you know it.

00:16:18.278 --> 00:16:19.863
You really hurt his feelings.

00:16:19.947 --> 00:16:21.949
Don't girl me with that girl stuff.

00:16:22.241 --> 00:16:23.575
Bender and me are guys.

00:16:23.659 --> 00:16:24.993
Guys don't have feelings.

00:16:25.285 --> 00:16:28.038
Bender's not a guy, he's a robot.

00:16:28.121 --> 00:16:29.623
Same thing.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:35.921
It's so big and empty.

00:16:38.423 --> 00:16:41.885
My roommate's gone,
and all he left behind was

00:16:41.969 --> 00:16:44.513
an eyelash
and three skin flakes.

00:16:51.353 --> 00:16:53.397
Aw... What's the point?

00:16:59.152 --> 00:17:00.279
Bender?

00:17:00.362 --> 00:17:02.656
My God, you're a mess.

00:17:05.942 --> 00:17:07.819
leave me alone.

00:17:08.153 --> 00:17:09.863
Look at that five o'clock rust.

00:17:10.363 --> 00:17:12.699
You've been up all night
not drinking, haven't you?

00:17:12.824 --> 00:17:16.161
Hey... What I don't do
is none of your business.

00:17:16.244 --> 00:17:18.246
Please, Bender,
have some malt liquor,

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:21.124
if not for yourself, then
for the people who love you.

00:17:21.208 --> 00:17:24.377
I hate the people who love me,
and they hate me.

00:17:24.878 --> 00:17:26.129
Oh, now, look.

00:17:26.213 --> 00:17:28.465
It's obvious you miss being Fry's roommate

00:17:28.548 --> 00:17:31.134
but there's got to be a better way
to deal with this.

00:17:31.159 --> 00:17:34.120
Like how,
having my antenna removed?

00:17:34.387 --> 00:17:36.041
Well... If that would work.

00:17:36.066 --> 00:17:39.989
Are you crazy? That's little Bender
you're talking about.

00:17:40.014 --> 00:17:41.474
I can't cut it off.

00:17:41.937 --> 00:17:45.398
You're not a robot or a man,
so you wouldn't understand.

00:17:45.899 --> 00:17:47.609
I got to get out of here.

00:17:47.692 --> 00:17:48.860
Wait.

00:17:48.944 --> 00:17:50.654
I want you to look me in the eye

00:17:50.821 --> 00:17:52.906
and promise you won't
get behind the wheel

00:17:53.008 --> 00:17:55.761
without some kind of alcoholic
beverage in your hand.

00:17:55.824 --> 00:17:58.535
I promise nothing!

00:18:27.941 --> 00:18:29.151
I don't even want to...

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.271
Why is...

00:18:37.242 --> 00:18:39.035
What up?

00:18:39.119 --> 00:18:41.621
I can't just stand by and be silent
about Bender anymore.

00:18:41.705 --> 00:18:45.125
Silent? You've been meddling
for two solid weeks.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:47.335
Well, I can't just do that anymore.

00:18:47.419 --> 00:18:49.337
Your best friend is out there somewhere

00:18:49.421 --> 00:18:50.505
destroying himself.

00:18:50.797 --> 00:18:52.299
Really?

00:18:52.382 --> 00:18:54.551
I didn't think he'd miss
this apartment that much.

00:18:54.634 --> 00:18:56.428
He doesn't care
about the apartment.

00:18:56.511 --> 00:18:59.347
He cares about you, and
you turned your back on him.

00:18:59.848 --> 00:19:01.684
Oh, man, I had no idea.

00:19:01.843 --> 00:19:04.144
If only I knew where he was,
I'd go talk to him.

00:19:05.662 --> 00:19:07.873
Oh, stupid TV.

00:19:09.082 --> 00:19:11.418
Bender.
You're blind stinking sober.

00:19:11.501 --> 00:19:13.920
That's right. I'm sober and crazy

00:19:14.004 --> 00:19:15.672
and I don't know what I might do.

00:19:15.756 --> 00:19:18.550
- Don't do it.
- I don't know what it is yet.

00:19:18.634 --> 00:19:20.636
Oh, yeah, now I remember.

00:19:20.719 --> 00:19:23.597
I thought I could live alone,
but I can't

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:27.976
so I'm going to do what it takes
to be your roommate again.

00:19:28.268 --> 00:19:29.686
Bender, stop.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.272
Cutting Leela's head off
won't solve anything.

00:19:32.356 --> 00:19:34.942
No, I'm going to chop off my antenna.

00:19:35.025 --> 00:19:37.069
Hey... Yeah, that sounds good.

00:19:37.152 --> 00:19:38.403
Can I give you a hand?

00:19:38.487 --> 00:19:41.031
Fry, don't help him
mutilate himself.

00:19:41.114 --> 00:19:42.491
But it's a useless antenna.

00:19:42.574 --> 00:19:44.952
It's not like he's
a ham radio or something.

00:19:45.035 --> 00:19:46.161
I'm going to do it!

00:19:46.244 --> 00:19:48.330
I'm really going to do it!

00:19:48.622 --> 00:19:50.165
Don't try and stop me!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.918
Here goes!

00:19:54.044 --> 00:19:56.213
Ohh...

00:20:03.136 --> 00:20:04.137
Hey, it worked.

00:20:04.221 --> 00:20:05.263
The static's gone.

00:20:05.555 --> 00:20:08.100
I hate that this came
between us, Calculon.

00:20:08.183 --> 00:20:09.351
Me, too.

00:20:09.434 --> 00:20:12.521
I'm filled with a large number of
powerful emotions.

00:20:12.604 --> 00:20:14.189
You're my best friend.

00:20:14.273 --> 00:20:16.191
I'm sorry
I treated you so badly.

00:20:16.275 --> 00:20:17.734
Apology accepted.

00:20:17.818 --> 00:20:20.320
After all, you're only human.

00:20:22.656 --> 00:20:25.575
You guys could learn a
lesson from those two.

00:20:25.659 --> 00:20:26.785
She's right.

00:20:26.868 --> 00:20:28.996
You're my best friend, Fry.

00:20:29.079 --> 00:20:31.623
I'm sorry
I treated you so badly.

00:20:31.707 --> 00:20:33.166
Apology accepted.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.419
After all,
you're only human.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:37.757
Wait a minute.

00:20:38.003 --> 00:20:39.504
You did it all backwards.

00:20:40.382 --> 00:20:41.717
Fry's the one who should be...

00:20:42.759 --> 00:20:44.136
Oh, never mind.

00:20:47.723 --> 00:20:49.391
Oh...

00:20:49.516 --> 00:20:51.685
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

00:20:51.768 --> 00:20:55.647
I guess I'm just going to have to get
used to being half a robot.

00:20:55.731 --> 00:20:56.732
Aw, this isn't right.

00:20:56.815 --> 00:20:59.109
Listen, Bender, if
we found your antenna,

00:20:59.192 --> 00:21:00.736
could they still reattach it?

00:21:00.819 --> 00:21:04.615
Maybe, if we get it on ice
right away.

00:21:06.408 --> 00:21:07.576
Bingo.

00:21:07.659 --> 00:21:11.580
Hmm. You call
that an antenna?

00:21:15.542 --> 00:21:18.629
This time you'll have
all the human comforts.

00:21:18.712 --> 00:21:20.881
We'll get a couple of toilets,

00:21:20.964 --> 00:21:23.884
some food cookers,
maybe a puppy...

00:21:28.138 --> 00:21:29.389
It's good to be home.

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:30.682
It sure is.

00:21:30.766 --> 00:21:32.559
By the way,
I saved your stuff.

00:21:32.643 --> 00:21:35.270
So that's where
those skin flakes went.

00:21:35.562 --> 00:21:37.356
Hmm. You think this fruit tree's

00:21:37.439 --> 00:21:38.459
going to get enough light?

00:21:38.574 --> 00:21:40.259
There's a window in the closet.

00:21:41.343 --> 00:21:44.305
Whoa.

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:45.681
This is huge.

00:21:45.764 --> 00:21:47.891
Bender, why don't
I just live in here?

00:21:47.975 --> 00:21:49.893
In a closet?

00:21:49.977 --> 00:21:51.562
Oh, humans.